# ============================================================
# debugger-workstation .gitignore
# 本仓库只放骨架/文档/manifest/自研代码,绝不放第三方工具二进制、
# 凭据、样本、缓存或本机状态。以下规则是硬边界。
# ============================================================

# --- 凭据与私密 (最高优先级,绝不入库) ---
.env
.env.*
*.env
**/.env
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.token
*token*
*secret*
*credential*
id_rsa*
*.ovpn

# --- 第三方工具二进制 / 大体积运行物 (靠 bootstrap 拉取,不入库) ---
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.jar
*.bin
*.msi
*.apk
*.dex
*.aab

# --- 压缩包 / 分发产物 ---
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.gz

# --- 运行时 / 虚拟环境 / 依赖 (体积大,可重建) ---
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
bin/Debug/
bin/Release/
obj/
publish/
Runtime/
dotnet/
dotnet-home/
nuget-packages/
apache-maven-*/

# --- MCP 临时工作区 / 扫描数据 / 样本 ---
MCP/workspaces/
**/workspaces/
**/YaraFlux/data/
.codex_extracted/
*_tmp_*/
MCP_SMOKE_*/

# --- 用户样本 / 取证产物 (严禁) ---
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.dump
*.dmp
*.CT
*.ct
*.har

# --- 第三方 MCP 克隆目录 (由 bootstrap 按 manifest clone,不入库) ---
mcp/third-party/
mcp/ILSpy-Mcp/
mcp/ReClass.NET-MCP/
mcp/YaraFlux/
mcp/apktool-mcp-server/
mcp/cheatengine-mcp-bridge/
mcp/dnspy-mcp-extension/
mcp/dnspy-mcp/
mcp/frida-mcp/
mcp/ida-pro-mcp/
mcp/imhexMCP/
mcp/mcp-wireshark/
mcp/mcp7zop/
mcp/mobsf-mcp-server/
mcp/reqable-mcp/
mcp/radare2-mcp/
mcp/volatility3-mcp/
mcp/mcp-virustotal/
mcp/GhidraMCP/
mcp/jadx-mcp-server/
mcp/x64dbg-automate/
mcp/x64dbg-automate-pyclient/

# --- 本机生成的 MCP 客户端配置 (含绝对路径) ---
mcp/.mcp.json
mcp/codex-mcp-config.toml
/.mcp.json
/.cursor/mcp.json
local.json
OWNER.md

# --- 部署后的分类目录 / 报告 / 原始包 (骨架仓库不含) ---
/Static-Reversing/
/Debuggers/
/Mobile-Android/
/Network-HTTP/
/Unpackers-Game/
/System-Forensics/
/OriginalBase/
/Launchers/
/Reports/
/_download-stage/
LOCAL-THIS-PC.md
notes/2026-09-01-binary-cache.md
notes/2026-09-01-full-tool-download.md


# --- 本机开发历史 / IDE ---
.codegraph/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log

# EXCEPTION, and it is the only one. Rule R17 binds a probe to `evidence/probes/<id>.probe.log`
# by path AND sha256, which is the whole point: a hash of a file git refuses to carry is a hash
# the next window and the next machine cannot check. `assert-probes.py --save-evidence` writes
# one `.probe.log` and one `.control.log` per capability here, and nothing else writes here, so
# the whole directory is exempt rather than a hand-maintained list of filenames.
!evidence/probes/
!evidence/probes/*.log
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# --- Lab build output (2026-09-30) ---
# Compiled challenges and decompiler output. The charter forbids exporting
# decompiled C into git: it is derived from binaries, machine-generated, and
# it would bury the real sources. Sources live in challenges/*/src; technique
# notes and known answers are committed by hand, everything under out/ is not.
/crackme-corpus/out/
*.obj
*.pdb
*.ilk

# Generated lab payload. Self-authored (lab/payload/d12payload.c) and rebuilt
# deterministically by the loop every run, so committing the binary would only
# add a stale copy. Sources are tracked; build outputs are not.
forensics-lab/lab/payload/*.dll
forensics-lab/lab/payload/*.exe

# --- managed-lab / headless-lab build output (2026-09-30) ---
# Compiled samples, decompilations, hash manifests and Ghidra projects. The
# sources and the known answers are committed by hand; everything produced from
# them is not.
/managed-lab/out/
/headless-lab/out/
managed-lab/**/obj/
headless-lab/**/obj/

# --- probe-artifacts (2026-10-05) ---
# Written by scripts/probe_artifact.{py,mjs,ps1} during a run. Same category as the out/ rules
# above: regenerated every time the probe runs, and assert-probes checks it as "a file THIS RUN
# wrote" -- so a committed copy would be a stale claim about a past run, not evidence of one.
# The durable record is evidence/probes/*.probe.log plus its sha256 in capabilities.json, which
# R17 and R28 keep both in git and in HEAD.
/probe-artifacts/
/native-lab/out/
/web-reverse/out/
/crypto-lab/out/
/forensics-lab/out/
/net-reverse/out/
/mobile-lab/out/
/crackme-corpus/out/

# .agent/research duplicates docs/research -- the tracked copy is canonical.
.agent/research/

# mission.ps1 -Action Ablate writes a full mutated COPY of itself beside the original,
# because that copy must live in $PSScriptRoot to resolve manifests\ (mission.ps1:2103).
# Its `finally` deletes the copy on every normal exit, but a KILLED run -- which a context
# compaction is -- leaves a 2,200-line scaffold sitting in a tracked source directory, and a
# `git add -A` then commits it as though it were source. Measured: that is exactly what
# happened here. These files are never inputs and never evidence.
scripts/mission-ablate-*.ps1

# Editor auto-save and lock files. Measured 2026-10-05: opening README.md left
# README.md.id0 (16 KB), .id1 (40 KB), .nam (8 KB) and .til (8 KB) beside it -- GDB/emacs
# auto-save siblings, each a real copy of the file, all untracked, all noise. The earlier
# `*~` / `*.bak` rules cover a different editor's habit; this is the same category from a
# different tool, and it needs its own patterns because the suffixes are numeric.
*.id0
*.id1
*.id2
*.id3
*.nam
*.til
*.swp
*.swo
*~
# Emacs lock and auto-save dots
\#*\#
.\#*

# Ghidra's analyzeHeadless writes its logs beside wherever it was invoked from, so a run
# launched from the repo root leaves STRAY-EXTRA/ holding analyzeHeadless.log and .log.err.
# Measured 2026-10-05: 56 KB of it, and the directory's own name says what it is. Same
# category as the out/ rules -- regenerated every run, never an input, never evidence.
STRAY-EXTRA/

# redteam-v2/ and redteam-baseline/ are another line's experiment output (the launcher
# session's OMP-LC-REDTEAM1 workers -- 32/64 refs in the launcher session, 0 refs in the
# romantic/kiro sessions; corrected 2026-10-14 by a read-only station-users survey).
# Declared non-content rather than moved, because moving someone else's working tree is
# the riskier act. If that line decides to track them, delete these two lines.
/redteam-v2/
/redteam-baseline/

# _re-work/ holds 106 MB of driver samples -- runtime data, belongs on E: per the
# charter. Ignored so the working tree stops reporting it; not moved, it is in use.
/_re-work/

# A three-line throwaway I wrote on 2026-10-05 to run one probe by hand (a BOM-prefixed
# ps1 holding `node fuzz-lab/tools/loop.mjs --budget 40` and `exit $LASTEXITCODE`).
# assert-probes.py runs every command itself; the file was never referenced by anything.
